---
import A from "../components/A.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import { SCHOLAR } from "../data/links";

---

<Section id="about" title="About Me">
  <div>
    <div class="space-y-5 text-gray-600">
      <p class="t-lead">
        I am the <strong class="text-gray-800">Head of Computer-Using Agents (CUA)</strong> at <strong class="text-gray-800">Beipo (北坡)</strong>,
        where I lead <A href="#northcua">NorthCUA</A> from zero to one: an experience-driven loop that connects a unified agent harness,
        experience data, model training and continual learning for agents that operate real desktop software and the web. Its open Nano,
        Mini and Pro models are state-of-the-art among open-source models (under the reported settings) in GUI grounding, desktop execution
        and web interaction. I am also responsible for the CUA and Web Agent capabilities of
        <A href="https://nex-agi.com">Nex-N2.5</A>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before that, I was a <strong class="text-gray-800">Principal Researcher</strong> in the Data, Knowledge and Intelligence
        <strong class="text-gray-800">(DKI)</strong> group at <strong class="text-gray-800">Microsoft</strong>, where I was the lead developer and
        algorithm researcher of <A href="https://github.com/microsoft/UFO/">UFO</A>, the first open-source Windows GUI agent / CUA framework, and
        drove its evolution through UFO² and UFO³ into a cross-platform, cross-device Desktop AgentOS with
        <strong class="text-gray-800">10K+ GitHub stars</strong>. I also worked on AIOps: anomaly detection, failure diagnosis and root cause
        analysis for cloud services. I maintain a public <A href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2411.18279">survey</A> on LLM-brained GUI agents
        (<A href="https://vyokky.github.io/LLM-Brained-GUI-Agents-Survey/">Website</A>) and wrote the first book that systematically
        introduces GUI agents. My work has been cited over <strong class="text-gray-800">8,100</strong> times on
        <A href={SCHOLAR}>Google Scholar</A>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Earlier, I was a research scientist at Lightspeed and Quantum Studio <strong class="text-gray-800">(光子工作室)</strong>, Tencent, where I
        developed matchmaking systems for the game <i>League of Legends: Wild Rift</i>. I hold a PhD from the School of Informatics at the
        University of Edinburgh, supervised by <A href="https://homepages.inf.ed.ac.uk/ppatras/">Prof. Paul Patras</A> and
        <A href="https://homepages.inf.ed.ac.uk/rsarkar/">Rik Sarkar</A>, an MSc in Artificial Intelligence from the same institution, and a
        BEng in Telecommunication Engineering from Huazhong University of Science and Technology.
      </p>
      <p>For any inquiries, please feel free to reach me at <strong class="text-gray-800">vyokky at 163 dot com</strong>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
